## 1. 📌 Lesson Overview — Deadlines, Updates & Follow-Ups

Professional communication across software engineering, quality assurance, and agile delivery centers around four functional communication pillars:

* ⚡ **Current Execution Status:** Articulating immediate priorities and ongoing activities using structured progressive chunks (e.g., `I'm currently working on...`).
* ⏱️ **Schedule & Cadence Management:** Transparently reporting timeline status—whether tasks are progressing as planned (`on track`), delayed (`behind schedule`), or recovered after impediment remediation (`back on track`).
* 🚧 **Blocker & Dependency Escalation:** Objectively highlighting external dependencies without friction or hostility (e.g., `I'm still waiting for...`).
* 🔄 **Action Item Governance:** Coordinating proactive alignment through structured checkpoints (`follow up on`) and formally closing discussion loops or delivery milestones (`wrap up`).

